.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt MOOBFS-CHECK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm moobfs-check
.Nd validate the typed MoobFS attributes of a tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -domain-depth Ar N
.Ar directory
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
walks
.Ar directory ,
a plain directory or a mounted MoobFS layer, validates every typed attribute and the format
marker on its root, and prints one JSON object with a
.Dq format
member and a list of
.Dq problems .
It diagnoses only and never repairs.
MoobFS is an experimental research project.
.Pp
With
.Fl -domain-depth Ar N ,
the depth of domain directories given to the layer as a mount option,
it also lists under
.Dq left_out
the files carrying typed attributes that QUERY2 does not return, with the reason: they fail the
homogeneity rule, or sit above every domain.
These are not problems and do not change the exit status.
.Pp
The JSON object also includes
.Dq files ,
.Dq typed_attributes ,
.Dq identities ,
.Dq identity_conflicts ,
.Dq same_id_other_namespace
and
.Dq problem_count
integer counts.
Each problem has string
.Dq path ,
.Dq attribute
and
.Dq problem
members.
With
.Fl -domain-depth ,
the object also has integer
.Dq domain_depth
and
.Dq left_out_count ,
plus a
.Dq left_out
array of path and reason strings.
The full schema and example are in docs/tools.md.
The JSON shape is experimental and may change.
.Pp
Below
.Ar directory
no symbolic link is followed, not even one put in place of a directory while the walk runs:
each entry is opened relative to its directory's descriptor and judged and read through that
descriptor, so the tool can be run as root over a tree that other users can write.
A symbolic link given as
.Ar directory
is not walked, and entries on other filesystems are skipped.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 2n -compact
.It 0
clean
.It 1
the tree could not be walked; the reason is printed
.It 2
problems found
.It 64
usage error, or
.Ar N
outside 1 to 32
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr moobfs-attr 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-index 1
.Pp
docs/tools.md and docs/spec-query-v2.md in the MoobFS repository,
.Lk https://github.com/studiomoob/llmoobfs
